    "note": "PRIORITY RAISED 12 -> 45, 2026-08-11. Planting this zone did nothing until now: at 12 it lost everywhere to z02_mesic_prairie (22) and z01_wet_prairie (20), which are ELEVATION BANDS matching the general plain, so the beach and the foredune were being rendered as mesic prairie. A zone defined by a specific geography and a specific SUBSTRATE has to outrank a band defined by height alone — the same reasoning that already puts the settled town (60) and the marsh (70) above both prairies. 45 keeps it below the marsh, the town and the sedge meadow, which is right: where the river mouth is marsh it is marsh, and where the fort stands it is settled ground, beach or no beach. PLANTABLE SINCE 2026-08-11. This community was written and then withheld: the ground it describes did not exist in the model. ROADMAP S2e has since extended the heightfield east from a 640 m square to E -320..+1700, and this zone's extent now matches 7,353 samples of the committed terrain, so it is planted. Nothing about the species, the July phenology or the confidence has changed — the records were always ready and the ground was not. WHAT THE ORIGINAL NOTE SAID, kept because it was correct when it was written: PLANTABLE SINCE 2026-08-11, when ROADMAP S2e parcel (b) carried the heightfield east to E +1700: the lake shore, the beach face and the sand bar are modelled ground now, so this community has something to stand on. The box is the belt east of the sand-ridge crest, bounded north and south by the scene's own span; the beach continues well beyond it. NOT FIXED HERE, for the flora parcel: at priority 12 this zone loses everywhere to z02_mesic_prairie (priority 22), whose 1.18-3.0 m elevation band now covers the whole sand belt, so the beach and the bar are currently planted as mesic prairie. The priorities were set when nothing east of E +320 had ground under it and the question could not arise."
  },
