  "note": "1835-specific and easy to get wrong: the harbour cut and piers were finished in 1834 and sand was accreting north of the north pier, so the lakefront just north of the river mouth is RAW BARE SAND, at most colonised by annual pioneers, not established marram turf. Bare sand is 85-98 per cent of the active beach surface (8a); the 55 per cent here is the average across beach, foredune and back-dune.",
